,"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Chatham County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years. In 2025, November to December finished at 44% of normal on the middle of the grids. In 2026 so far, the middle of the grids shows March to April at 37% and April to May at 39%. July to August is the wettest pair at 9.52 inches of normal, and October to November is the driest at 6.42 inches.</p>"}
